// =============================================================================
// Maple Bay — RELATIONSHIPS: the people  (src/story/rel_people.js)          PURE DATA. No engine imports, no init(), no side effects.
// The ten romanceable people, the twelve vignette-arc people, and Porchlight (the dating app).
// EVERY person here already exists in src/story/cast.js (same id, name, look, routine, home, birthday). Nothing is cloned or renamed:
// this file only ADDS what the relationship systems need. Dad (`dad`) is added to the cast at load by sim/_chapters_cast.js.
// Design: docs/story/RELATIONSHIPS.md sections 5-8. Verified by `node tools/rel_check.mjs`.
//
// EXPORTS
//   ROMANCEABLE   string[10]  ids, in the order of the bible.
//   ARC_PEOPLE    string[12]  ids of the people with a vignette arc (rel_arcs_a.js / rel_arcs_b.js); 'kids' = Pip and Milo together.
//   PEOPLE        { [id]: Person }   romanceables and arc people.
//   PORCHLIGHT    the dating app: screens, the player's own card, filters, matching rules, chat rules.
//
// PERSON (all)
//   id, kind: 'romance' | 'family' | 'friend'
//   craft        skill id they can show you (VERBS_NEW show_me), or null
//   likes        { recipes: recipeId[], gifts: giftId[] (cast.js GIFTS, repeated here so one file answers "what do they like"),
//                  outings: dateTypeId[] (rel_dates.js DATE_TYPES; friends use them for plus-ones), places: placeId[] }
//   dislikes     { recipes?, outings? }
//   keyLine      what they say when keys are traded (friend: swap_keys; romance: before their `keys` scene)
//   advice       { work, home, heart, family }  one line each for the `advice` verb
//   giftNotes    { [giftId]: line }  said a day or two after a loved gift ("gift_notes")
// PERSON (romance) adds
//   age, pronouns   (as cast.js; repeated for the app card)
//   work         { venue, title, bossOf?: jobId }      home: { cast: cast.js home id, anchor: a real door the engine can use, address: words }
//   free         [{ days: weekday[] (0 = Mon), from, to }]   when they can be asked on a date (their cast routine is busy outside this)
//   looks        { date: spec overrides, home: spec overrides }  on top of their cast.js spec; every part is in art/chars lists
//   inner        the thing they are working through (their heart scenes are about this, not about the player)
//   bossLine / bossLine2   only for people who are a job's boss        ageLine   only for the three older people
//   missed       their reply to the miss_you verb
//   profile      { headline, about, prompts: [[question, answer] x3], photos: [caption x3], looking }   their Porchlight card
//   chat         { known: string[] (their first message if you have already met in town), fresh: string[] (if you have not),
//                  asks: [[what the player can send, their reply] x4], yes: their reply when a first date is proposed }
// =============================================================================

